/Title (2. Non-Primitive Data Structure :- A non-primitive data structure is a complex data structure built from primitive data types that is used to store and organize multiple data elements efficiently. It is classified to two types         Linear Data Structure - Linear data structures            organize data in a sequential manner where each element   is adjacent to the previous one.  Ex:- Array, Linked List, Stack, Queue          Non-Linear Data Structure - Non-linear data structures organize data hierarchically, connecting elements in a more complex, branching manner.  Ex:- Tree, Graph)
